# Binary files this repo commits on purpose. One bash glob per line.
#
# Read by scripts/check_no_binaries.sh. Note that matching uses bash `case`,
# where `*` DOES cross `/` -- so `Programming/*.pdf` matches a .pdf at any
# depth under Programming/.
#
# Policy for this repo (approved decision 3). This is an archive of submitted
# university coursework: the reports, figures, schematics and datasets ARE the
# deliverable, so they stay, and history is not rewritten. What the gate is
# actually here to stop is NEW junk -- compiled output, and binaries dropped
# into the tooling directories.
#
# So the allowlist is scoped by PATH, not blanket:
#   - documents/figures/data are allowed under Programming/ and NotProgramming/
#   - compiled output (.o .so .a .exe .dll .dylib .class .pyc .pyo) is allowed
#     NOWHERE, and has no entry below. 189 such files were untracked in
#     d4075278; .gitignore keeps them out.
#   - the repo root, gates/, scripts/ and .github/ have no entry either, so a
#     binary added there is blocked.
#
# Every pattern here must also survive `git ls-files | git check-ignore
# --stdin --no-index` printing nothing -- an allowlisted file that .gitignore
# also matches fails silently on `git add` rather than erroring.

# --- Reports and presentations (155 .pdf, 3 .docx, 1 .doc, 1 .pptx) ---------
Programming/*.pdf
NotProgramming/*.pdf
Programming/*.doc
NotProgramming/*.doc
Programming/*.docx
NotProgramming/*.docx
Programming/*.ppt
NotProgramming/*.ppt
Programming/*.pptx
NotProgramming/*.pptx

# --- Figures, screenshots, schematics (275 .png, 68 .jpg, 52 .gif, ...) -----
Programming/*.png
NotProgramming/*.png
Programming/*.jpg
NotProgramming/*.jpg
Programming/*.jpeg
NotProgramming/*.jpeg
Programming/*.gif
NotProgramming/*.gif
Programming/*.bmp
NotProgramming/*.bmp
Programming/*.svg
NotProgramming/*.svg
Programming/*.webp
NotProgramming/*.webp
Programming/*.ico
NotProgramming/*.ico
Programming/*.tif
NotProgramming/*.tif
Programming/*.tiff
NotProgramming/*.tiff

# --- Fonts shipped inside a submitted project ------------------------------
Programming/*.ttf
NotProgramming/*.ttf

# --- Datasets and course-supplied archives ---------------------------------
# The .tgz entries matter: EOPSY ships its simulators as ftp/sched.tgz and
# ftp/memory.tgz, and `make setup` extracts them. Blocking those would break
# the lab. The .zip files are submitted result bundles and course inputs.
Programming/*.zip
NotProgramming/*.zip
Programming/*.tgz
NotProgramming/*.tgz
Programming/*.bin
NotProgramming/*.bin
